// ICSE 2027 — a MINIMAL venue preset: the conference NLBSE 2027, AGENT 2027 and AGENTVERIFY 2027
// are held at, so they can name it as their `parent`. It carries the edition's names and its
// template family, and no page limit or deadline: it exists so its workshops can name it, not as
// the research track's preset. Its card: `icse-2027.md`.
//
// Verbatim from https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2027/icse-2027-research-track (fetched
// 2026-11-19): «All submissions must conform to the IEEE conference proceedings template,
// specified in the IEEE Conference Proceedings Formatting Guidelines (title in 24pt font and full
// text in 10pt type, LaTeX users must use \documentclass[10pt,conference]{IEEEtran} without
// including the compsoc or compsocconf options). Note that IEEE format is being used this year,
// whereas last year it was ACM format.»
//
// 🔴 THE TEMPLATE FLIPS BETWEEN EDITIONS: ICSE 2027 is IEEE, ICSE 2028 is ACM (icse-2028.jsonc).
// Its workshops follow ICSE 2027's: NLBSE «All submissions must conform to the ICSE’27 formatting
// and submission instructions», AGENTVERIFY «IEEE format in line with ICSE 2027», AGENT «the IEEE
// conference proceedings template».
{
  "type": "venue",
  // The series, without a year: the year is the id's (icse-2027), the one source of it.
  "name": "ICSE",
  // The research track's call quoted above.
  "url": "https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2027/icse-2027-research-track",
  "extends": "paperlint:ieee-conference",

  // What the Artifact Evaluation track asks an artifact to hold. Its workshops have no artifact
  // track of their own (AGENT's call says nothing about artifacts), so they take this bar through
  // `parent`. Verbatim from https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2027/icse-2027-artifact-evaluation
  // (read 2026-11-20):
  //   «Includes a README detailing the environment setup, data structure (if applicable), and usage
  //    examples.»
  //   «Each artifact repository must include the following materials: Accepted paper (PDF) - A copy
  //    of the accepted paper that includes a link to the archival repository where the artifact is
  //    hosted. LICENSE file - A clear description of the distribution rights. For artifacts seeking
  //    the Available badge, the license must permit public access and reuse.»
  //   «README file - Provided in Markdown, plain text, or PDF format»
  //   «In order to be eligible for the Artifacts Available badge, it must be placed in a repository
  //    with a permanence plan and a stable identifier (e.g., DOI).»
  // README and LICENSE are recorded. Not recorded: the accepted paper's PDF and the archival DOI —
  // both exist only after acceptance, and a review-time artifact is usually an anonymous link.
  "artifact_bar": {
    "source": "call",
    "url": "https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2027/icse-2027-artifact-evaluation",
    "read": "2026-11-20",
    "files": ["README", "LICENSE"],
  },
}
